<page type="text" lines="ocr">
  <layout>One page of verse, one column of italic lines; running head at top with page number 164 at top right.</layout>
  <page_number>164</page_number>
  <running_head>ABRA. SACRIFICANS.</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">
      <i>Fœcunda tellus, atque tegunt poli</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2">
      <i>Flammantis axes, quàm sariant sagū</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3">
      <i>Subiecta passim casibus omnia!</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4">
      <i>Nil magnus orbis despicit Arbiter</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5">
      <i>Ab arce summa, quod maneat diu.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">
      <i>Sed durat idem solus, si illius</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7">
      <i>Æternitatem secula non metunt.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>Non semper almum purpureis micans</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9">
      <i>Titan quadrigis irradiat diem,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>Verùm recedens Oceani cauis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11">
      <i>Se mergit sndis, mox sbi rosidæ,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>Et noctis atra prauiùs arduo</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>Candere Olympo cœperit Hesperus,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>Et furua clarum condere nox diem.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>Quàm mutat errans Luna polo suos</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>Subinde sultus! Quàm sarias globo</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17">
      <i>Nigrante formas induit! Aureo</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>Mox tota fulgens lumine cernitur:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19">
      <i>Mox parte tantùm dimidia nitet:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">
      <i>Mox sola monstrat cornua: mox suos</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21">
      <i>Abscondit orbes: nusquam eadem manet,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22">
      <i>Cursus nec sna flectere amat sia.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23">
      <i>Et clara cælo sydera quæ micant,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24">
      <i>Si saruientes excitat impotens</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25">
      <i>Auster procellas, aut gelidum suidis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="26">
      <i>Imbrem refundens nubibus ætherem</i>
    </l>
    <l n="27">
      <i>Obscuiat, ignes protinus occultant:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="28">
      <i>Et certa nautis signa frementibus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="29">
      <i>Monstrare cessant, quum ratibus mar</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Text is verse with long s throughout; some words doubtful due to print damage on the right edge and at the bottom line, marked [?] where unclear. Several words in the lines ("sagū", "ssnsidæ", "sna", "syda") are poorly printed and uncertain.</notes>
</page>
